nodes.append({
 "id": 6, "lang": "Persian", "words": "bâleš",
 "verdict": "confirmed",
 "derivation": "NP بالش bāleš 'pillow' is the straight continuation of MP bālišn, with loss of the final -n of the suffix; Wiktionary gives the chain بالش < MP 𐡡𐠠𐡫𐡱𐡭 (bʾlšn' /bālišn/) < Proto-Iranian *barjíš < Proto-Indo-Iranian *bʰarǵʰíš < PIE *bʰelǵʰ-, i.e. exactly Nourai's route and exactly Pokorny's bhelǵh-. The doublet بالین bālīn (the chart's 'extra'), now archaic and largely poetic, continues MP bālēn. The Ferdowsī line quoted in the chart (سرانجام خشتست بالین تو) shows the bālīn form in the Shāhnāma. Both are thus reflexes of Av. barəziš-/barəšnu- and cognate with Skt. barhis-, Old Prussian balsinis 'cushion', Serbo-Croat blàzina, Gothic balgs 'bag'.",
