 "verdict": "confirmed",
 "derivation": "NP بلوار bolvār (also spelled بولوار) is a 20th-century direct loan from French boulevard, taken in during the Reza Shah period together with the town-planning concept itself (the wide tree-lined avenue). Mo‘in's dictionary enters it as بولوار with the French tag and the definition 'میدان و خیابانی که باغچه‌ها و چمن‌ها و درختان سایه‌دار دارد و محل گردش عموم است', with the cross-reference 'بلوار'. French [bul-] is rendered بولـ/بلـ and the final -vard as -وار, the -d being dropped exactly as in the French pronunciation.",
